abstract: >-
  MELITE is a pre-stable comparative classifier evaluator for tabular
  classification, classifier selection with nested cross-validation, final model
  export, and artifact-based inference.

  It operates at the tabular modeling level by consuming numeric feature
  matrices and labels. MELITE evaluates SVC, Random Forest, XGBoost, and
  opt-in Stacking classifiers under an outer repeated-stratified
  cross-validation framework. Tunable classifiers are optimized with Optuna
  inside each outer training split, under the same declared trial budget across
  tunable classifiers. It selects the best active classifier by mean outer-CV
  F1-macro, persists aggregate and per-fold evaluation evidence together with
  per-search optimization evidence, and supports final model retraining, export,
  and artifact-based inference.
